          <zone h='10584' id='19' name='County median burden change | Contiguous U.S.' pane-specification-id='0' param='[federated.0dgypka0lcwoy41ckwlhk1q395w4].[med:burden_change_pp:qk]' type-v2='color' w='20919' x='79081' y='71774'>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='12' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='10585' id='20' type-v2='text' w='100000' x='0' y='89415'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#64748b' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='9'>Methodology:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#64748b' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='9'> Analysis covers a balanced panel of 2,486 U.S. counties observed annually from 2015–2024. Modeled mortgage payments assume a 20% down payment and 30-year fixed mortgage using annual average Freddie Mac mortgage rates. Payment burden equals annual principal-and-interest payments divided by Census SAIPE median household income. Estimates exclude property taxes, insurance, HOA fees, maintenance, and closing costs.</run>
              <run fontcolor='#64748b' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='9'>
Map: Each county is shaded by its 2015–2024 payment burden change. Color scale runs from −10 to +25 percentage points; values beyond those limits use the endpoint colors. Hover for exact values. State and county controls apply to the map. Alaska and Hawaii are outside the default view.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='12' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{C753AC78-6ABE-4703-AC67-B1B75CD8880A}' />
